{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/853963-background-on-king-albrecht","id":853963,"title":"Background on King Albrecht","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-27T03:48:12-07:00","id":853963,"title":"Background on King Albrecht","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> I'm starting a new WW campaign and one of my players want to play &quot;Albrecht's little cousin&quot;. I've research a bit on the Internet and it looks good to have my story going parallel to Albrecht's story. If I want to read everything about Albrecht, what books/novels/etc should I read?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:52:50-07:00","id":854028,"title":"","content":"Silver Crown, SilverFang TB:Revised, intro and extra comic in WTA 2nd Edition and some of the Tribe Novel series. On being part of his extended family it's totally a possibility (most of the SilverFang breeding genealogy means they are all something like 2nd or 3rd cousins within a House anyway) and its a nice way to loosely tie a character into the game background stories (I've played one of his Cousins who got, ironically, exiled for being an overly proud prick who ended up in brawls with some of the Sept and with Mari, so he got sent away to a mixed/Gnawer sept to learn something about the other tribes and stop being an entitled brat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T06:41:44-07:00","id":854451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/853963-background-on-king-albrecht?p=854028#post854028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S and some of the Tribe Novel series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read those like 10 years ago. Can you refresh my mind on what Albrecht has to do with them?<br /> I barely remember they are about a pack of young garous (none from Albrecht pack) who discovered something evil and traveled through several caerns to fight it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T09:56:38-07:00","id":854525,"title":"","content":"Features Mari fairly early on and her falling into a coma after an attack by a knowledge eating bane of the brood of Jacco'lath'mattric. Albrecht becomes embroiled with a chunk of the goings on once he learns of the situation and Karin Jarlsdottir calls for the Convocation. He ends up at the meeting at the Nightsky Sept with the Margrave, Tamara Tsaravich and Sergei Dawntreader and ends up in conflict with Arkady before Arkady dances the White Spiral and they lead a combined strike force against Jacco'lath'mattric physical form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:04:19-07:00","id":854913,"title":"","content":"Oh, that rings a bell. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T04:54:27-07:00","id":858892,"title":"","content":"Most of Albrechts early live is in Silver Crown and the comic-intro from 2nd Edition Werewolf.<br /> <br /> He was rapidly earning renown in his home sept. A sept run by his grand-father Jacob Morningkill, who happened to be the King of the Wyrmfoe house. Iirc, Silver Crown states that Morningkill was Albrechts Great-Grand-Father, but Morningkill wanted to be the grandfather of a garou (since none of his actual children bred true) and had in the records of the sept one generation removed from Albrechts linage. But that is not that important. Once the King grew threatened by his relative and feared he might be challenged he banished Albrecht, using the latter's disregard for etiquette as reason by declaring it insubordination and failure to submit. Albrecht then lived as a dis-disillusioned drunk in NYC.<br /> I cant remember if his first fight with Mari was before he was banished or after, however the both once clashed in a fight. However, when Falcon lead Albrecht to the new cub Evan and the events from the introduction comic unfold they end up being a three-person pack. No pack name or totem is given, iirc.<br /> In the meantime Baba Yaga rose in Russia and erected the Shadow Curtain. Arkady, a highly bred Silverfang was smuggled out of the Curtain by BSD. His yob was to rally the garou outside the Curtain to invade Russia and help. But he ended up at Morningkills court as a kind of permanent-resident foreign envoy and pack leader of the king's own - Morningkills former pack and basically the sept's questing pack (the one that gets all the cool missions). The BSD however want compensation for smuggling Arkady out, and invade the sept and kill the king.<br /> At this point the Seneshall sends for Albrecht who returns home. Arkady and Albrecht both claim the throne, a duel ends in Arkadys favour (through cheating, which conveniently nobody recognized). With everything lost, the Seneshall proclaims, that if Albrecht can find the silver crown, a legendary artifact, before the in-coronation, Arkadys claim is invalid. So Albrechts and his pack search for the lost artifact and eventually find it.<br /> He banishes Arkady back to Russia (and back into the Shadow Curtain), but tells nobody that he was a traitor or what really happened between them. His logic being (as revealed by an inner monologue if Mari's in Black Furies Tribe novel) being, that Arkady was a paragon of the tribe, pure breed 5+, a beacon of hope (unlike Albrecht). Revealing him as a traitor would crush the spirit of the tribe (or at least the Russian Silverfangs).<br /> Albrecht rules over the sept of Morningkill, in New York state, house Wyrmfoe nominally rules over the east coast of the US and Canada, and as the bearer of the Silver Crown, he nominally rules over all garou. However, Albrecht never uses this power (his quest to find the crows taught him, that this power used unwisely brought about the fall of house winter snow, and Falcon actually removed the ability to command any garou from the crown). His time as a drunk in NYC and contact to all the other tribes has left him in a position where he can put himself in another's shoes, also he is never condescending while retaining the social bonuses from his pure breed. This makes him a respected figure of authority amongst the septleaders and elders in the American east, while none of them would openly submit to him.<br /> <br /> Besides finding the silver Crown, his greatest accomplishment is acting against the 7th generation (a human/children exploiting wyrm cult). Another garou banished by Morningkill, Loba Carcassonne, had been tracking this cult for a long time. Albrecht believes her and the cult is destroyed. The cult or the means to destroy it are presented as something new to the Garou Nation, or somewhat groundbreaking, although I'm not sure why. I never read 'Rage across New York'. But, the destruction of the 7th Generation came with some insight that never shall be forgotten and therefore immortalized Albrecht and his pack by granting their tale entry into the Silver Records.<br /> <br /> So, aside from the Tribe Novels, this is what I can remember of Albrecht's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}